course: dictionary
lesson: 12760
title: Dyeing: changing colour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dyeing means changing the colour of something by soaking it in a coloured liquid called dye. You can dye cloth, wool, hair or even an Easter egg. «I am dyeing my scarf blue.» Here dyeing is the action, and the scarf ends up a new colour.
explain: Dyeing can be a verb, which shows an action, or a noun, which names a craft or job. «Dyeing is an old craft.» Here it means the skill of colouring cloth and wool. Look at the words around it to see which meaning the writer chose.
explain: The -ing ending often means something is happening right now, as in «We are dyeing eggs for Easter.» The base word is dye: dye, dyes, dyed, dyeing. A good check is to put "colouring with dye" into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Dyeing means changing the colour of something by soaking it in dye.
fact: Dye is the coloured liquid used to change the colour of cloth, wool, hair or eggs.
fact: «Dyeing» can be a verb: «She is dyeing her hair.»
fact: «Dyeing» can also be a noun for the craft of colouring cloth and wool.
fact: Long ago, people dyed cloth with plants such as onion skins and beetroot.
exercise: «I am dyeing my old T-shirt black.» What is happening to the T-shirt? | It is being washed in cold water | It is being folded neatly | *It is getting a new colour | It is being torn into strips
exercise: In art, we learned about dyeing cloth with onion skins. What does dyeing mean here? | Cutting paper into shapes | Drawing a picture | *Colouring cloth by soaking it in a coloured liquid | Sewing buttons on a coat
exercise: Ella says dyeing is only for hair. What is the best answer? | Yes, but only in summer | *No, cloth, wool and eggs can be dyed too | Yes, it is only for hair | No, it means cutting
test: «We spent the afternoon dyeing eggs with beetroot.» What are the children doing to the eggs? | Boiling them only | Peeling them | *Colouring them with dye | Hiding them
test: Which word means the craft of colouring cloth and wool? | sewing | *dyeing | knitting
exam: «Tie-dyeing makes bright patterns on cotton T-shirts.» What does tie-dyeing mean? | Sewing a T-shirt | *Making patterns by tying cloth and soaking it in dye | Tying shoelaces | Washing a T-shirt in hot water
